# Documentation and decisions

Current GitHub Wiki documentation is part of the human-facing implementation contract. Update a document when the implementation changes something that document is responsible for.

## Document roles

- [Architecture](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Architecture) — structural rules, ownership, invariants
- [Decisions and ADRs](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Decisions-and-ADRs) — Architecture Decision Records
- [Protocol](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Protocol) — wire protocol, trust, versioning
- [Roadmap](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Roadmap) — phase order, status, per-phase notes
- [Testing and Quality](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Testing-and-Quality) — recorded gates and how they were verified
- [Diagnostics and Presentation](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Diagnostics-and-Presentation) — living budgets and measurements (values may be TBD)
- [Content and Authoring](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Content-and-Authoring) — authoring, IDs, validation
- [Content and Authoring](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Content-and-Authoring) — entry point for authored and durable saves
- [Diagnostics and Presentation](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Diagnostics-and-Presentation) — client debug vs diagnostics split (D-track)
- [Diagnostics and Presentation](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Diagnostics-and-Presentation) — D-track slice order
- `README.md` — orientation and current status
- [Historical Archive](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Historical-Archive) — original bootstrap execution plan (historical)
- root `PHASE` — current phase marker

Keep these consistent with their intended roles. Avoid copying the same fact into many documents. Prefer one authoritative location for each durable truth. Volatile numbers belong in code and the document that owns them (often `PERFORMANCE_BUDGETS.md` or `PROTOCOL.md`), not in Cursor rules.

## Saving

Work that writes authored content or durable gameplay state reads [Content and Authoring](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Content-and-Authoring) first. Do not copy it into this rule. The change report includes a Persistence Impact note: data class, owner and commit boundary, what remains pending, stale state and retries, disconnect and restart, whether a content, database, or protocol migration is needed, and which tests prove it.

## ADRs

ADR = Architecture Decision Record: a durable record of an important architectural decision, its reasoning, and relevant alternatives/tradeoffs.

Process lives in [Decisions and ADRs](https://github.com/Arieltetenboim/Purgatory/wiki/Decisions-and-ADRs). Status values: `accepted`, `superseded`, `deferred`.

Create or update an ADR for significant architectural decisions (authority, protocol, identity, persistence, concurrency, major dependencies, crate boundaries).

Do **not** create ADRs for ordinary implementation details (local helpers, numeric tuning that docs already treat as configuration, test arrangement).

## Conflicts

If documentation and implementation materially disagree:

1. Do not silently choose whichever is convenient.
2. Identify the inconsistency.
3. Determine whether the current task includes resolving it.
4. Report unresolved conflicts clearly.

Do not rewrite existing project documentation merely to match agent rules. Rules must reflect the project; they must not redefine it.
